er paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-two-channel-cap"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-two-channel-cap"],"id":"long.thm-two-channel-cap","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.3 (Two-channel and dyadic cap sufficiency)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.3, p. 45, label thm:two-channel-cap","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose that for every $n\\ge0$ at which the next weight is skipped,\n$$\nw_{n+1}>r_n(1/2)\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n r_n(1/2)\\le 2^{-(n+1)}+\\frac13\\,4^{-(n+1)}.\n$$\nThen $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$. The stronger bound $r_n(1/2)\\le2^{-(n+1)}$ at the same skipped ranks also suffices. The first bound retains two positive geometric terms of the full tail; it is larger, and hence less restrictive, than the second. Both are sufficient tests on the specified greedy orbit. The result does not assert that either bound holds at all its skipped ranks.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-two-channel-cap","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-two-channel-cap","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-two-channel-cap%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_skipped_dyadicCap%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-two-channel-cap%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_skipped_dyadicCap%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_of_skipped_dyadicCap"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0